1|"""Tests for the review & edit screen — app/static/preview.js.
2|
3|The page is where "which control is wired to what" lives, and that is a real
4|place for bugs: the first cut of the quantity stepper handed focus back to
5|whichever search box you had last touched, which popped its typeahead list open.
6|Nothing in the Python suite could see that.
7|
8|So these drive the actual file through a small DOM shim (`preview_dom.js`) in
9|whatever JavaScript engine the machine has — macOS ships JavaScriptCore — and
10|skip cleanly when there isn't one. They assert two things per interaction: what
11|was saved, and what got the focus afterwards.
